The legal text comes from the Présidence de la République du Tchad (https://presidence.td/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/Constitution.pdf), retrieved on 29 October 2026. The Présidence states no licence for the legal text. It is an official legal text; its copyright status is not confirmed here, and it is reproduced with the attribution above.

The Code pénal (loi n° 2017-01 du 8 mai 2017, also cited as loi n° 001/PR/2017 portant Code pénal) is copied from the PDF held by FAOLEX (https://faolex.fao.org/docs/pdf/cha213367.pdf), retrieved on 30 October 2026. The PDF carries a droit-afrique.com running head and states no licence.

The Code du travail (loi n° 038/PR/96 du 11 décembre 1996) is copied from the text held in the ILO NATLEX database (https://www.ilo.org/dyn/natlex/docs/WEBTEXT/47297/65070/F96TCD01.htm), as archived by the Internet Archive on 2 October 2017, retrieved on 30 October 2026. Chad is a member of OAPI, and Article 6(i) of Annex VII of the Bangui Agreement excludes official texts of a legislative nature from copyright protection.

Changes made by Lexifina: the text was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per line; spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised; footnotes, running heads and page numbers were removed; and the text was arranged as git commits. The wording of the law was not changed. The Présidence de la République du Tchad does not endorse this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
